@*
    _AutosaveIndicator.cshtml — Spec 021 / T054 / R-5 / FR-016 autosave UX.

    Renders the four states of the per-field autosave indicator:
      - idle    : hidden
      - saving  : "Guardando…"
      - saved   : "✓ Guardado HH:MM"
      - failed  : "⚠ No guardado — reintentar"

    State is driven by the `data-autosave-state` attribute on the wrapper,
    toggled by `autosave.js` on blur/response. All four state elements are
    rendered up-front; CSS-style attribute selectors (via Tabler `d-none`
    fallback class) hide the inactive ones. Vanilla JS — no framework binding.

    Markup expectations:
      - The wrapper element is targeted by `autosave.js` via the
        `[data-autosave-indicator]` selector.
      - The retry button carries `[data-autosave-retry]` so the script can rebind.
*@
<span class="fl-autosave-indicator" data-autosave-indicator data-autosave-state="idle" role="status" aria-live="polite">
    <span class="autosave-idle text-muted d-none" data-state-for="idle"></span>
    <span class="autosave-saving text-muted d-none" data-state-for="saving">Guardando…</span>
    <span class="autosave-saved text-success d-none" data-state-for="saved">
        <i class="ti ti-check me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        Guardado
        <time data-saved-at></time>
    </span>
    <span class="autosave-failed text-danger d-none" data-state-for="failed">
        <i class="ti ti-alert-triangle me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        No guardado &mdash;
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link btn-sm p-0 ms-1" data-autosave-retry>reintentar</button>
    </span>
</span>
